"]}," ",{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"social-share-trigger"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"5","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"6","cy":"12","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"19","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"8.59","x2":"15.42","y1":"13.51","y2":"17.49"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"15.41","x2":"8.59","y1":"6.51","y2":"10.49"},"children":[]}]},"Share this tip"]}]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-detail-toggle","aria-expanded":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"10","height":"10","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"currentColor","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]}]},"Hide details"]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-down rotated","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6 9 6 6 6-6"},"children":[]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-details"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["No cost involved. If you see unfamiliar metal cylinders, lead containers, or parts removed from equipment, simply steer clear — don’t pick them up, take them apart, or put them in your pocket."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["As of 2025, roughly 178,000 radioactive sources and 355,000 radiation devices are in use nationwide. The annual rate of radiation incidents involving sources remains below one per 10,000 sources. Classification is as follows: loss, theft, or uncontrolled release of Category I or II sources constitutes a major radiation incident; Category III is a relatively serious incident. Loss or theft of Category IV or V sources, or exposure exceeding annual dose limits, counts as a minor incident. Official example: In June 2020, a γ‑ray inspection was performed during pipeline upgrades at a steel plant in Ningxia. A Category II iridium‑192 source exposed three workers to radiation; one suffered third‑degree acute skin damage, another had fourth‑degree injuries on several fingers, and a third had first‑ to second‑degree burns. All three received doses far above legal limits; both responsible firms had their radiation licenses revoked and were fined 70,000 yuan. International example: In 1987, 50.8 TBq of cesium‑137 was removed from a radiotherapy machine in Goiânia, Brazil, after the device was dismantled; the source’s protective casing was ruptured. About 112,000 people were screened; 249 showed internal or external contamination, 129 of whom required moderate to severe medical care. Four people ultimately died. (National and international statistics)"]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Original sources"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":["生态环境部 (2025). 2024 中国生态环境状况公报. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.mee.gov.cn/ywgz/sthjjcgl/hjzljcypj/202506/t20250605_1120773.shtml","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://www.mee.gov.cn/ywgz/sthjjcgl/hjzljcypj/202506/t20250605_1120773.shtml"]},"；国家核安全局 (2026). 2025 年我国核与辐射安全监管工作成效. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://nnsa.mee.gov.cn/tpxw/202601/t20260107_1140062.html","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://nnsa.mee.gov.cn/tpxw/202601/t20260107_1140062.html"]},"；生态环境部 (2021). 关于一起 γ 射线探伤作业违法违规造成辐射事故案件处理情况的通报. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.mee.gov.cn/xxgk2018/xxgk/xxgk06/202101/t20210121_818216.html","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://www.mee.gov.cn/xxgk2018/xxgk/xxgk06/202101/t20210121_818216.html"]},"；国务院 (2019). 放射性同位素与射线装置安全和防护条例（2019 年修订，第三十四、四十二、六十八条）. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.mee.gov.cn/ywgz/fgbz/xzfg/201909/t20190918_734315.shtml","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://www.mee.gov.cn/ywgz/fgbz/xzfg/201909/t20190918_734315.shtml"]},"；环境保护部 (2009). 关于建立放射性同位素与射线装置辐射事故分级处理和报告制度的通知（辐射事故分级标准）. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.mee.gov.cn/gkml/zj/wj/200910/t20091022_172414.htm","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://www.mee.gov.cn/gkml/zj/wj/200910/t20091022_172414.htm"]},"；International Atomic Energy Agency (1988). The Radiological Accident in Goiânia. IAEA, Vienna. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www-pub.iaea.org/MTCD/Publications/PDF/Pub815_web.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://www-pub.iaea.org/MTCD/Publications/PDF/Pub815_web.pdf"]},"；王福如, 王进, 余宁乐, 等 (2019). 南京“5.7”放射源丢失事故受照者照后医学随访观察. 中华放射医学与防护杂志, 39(11), 859-863. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.3760/cma.j.issn.0254-5098.2019.11.011","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.3760/cma.j.issn.0254-5098.2019.11.011"]},"；中国环境报 (2014-05-15). 放射源丢失的48小时（徐小怗、邵艺、褚方樵、汤景茹）. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"http://nnsa.mee.gov.cn/ztzl/haqshmhsh/hjbzl/202406/P020240624472937009953.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["http://nnsa.mee.gov.cn/ztzl/haqshmhsh/hjbzl/202406/P020240624472937009953.pdf"]},"（网页存档 ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://web.archive.org/web/20261005044102/http://nnsa.mee.gov.cn/ztzl/haqshmhsh/hjbzl/202406/P020240624472937009953.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://web.archive.org/web/20261005044102/http://nnsa.mee.gov.cn/ztzl/haqshmhsh/hjbzl/202406/P020240624472937009953.pdf"]},"）"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.mee.gov.cn/ywgz/sthjjcgl/hjzljcypj/202506/t20250605_1120773.shtml","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"life-source-link"},"children":["Open source link"," ",{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"13","height":"13","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M15 3h6v6"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M10 14 21 3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"},"children":[]}]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Book note"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-content-reference"},"children":["If you actually find one: keep your distance, remember the location, do not move it, and call 110. Regulations require reporting it to the ecology and environment authorities, police, and health authorities. Distance and time are the only effective protection; a pocket or plastic bag provides none. X-ray machines and CT scanners produce radiation using electricity and do not remain radioactive after the power is switched off. The real danger is the sealed radioactive source inside equipment. Hospital radiotherapy machines, gamma-ray inspection equipment used on pipes and boilers, well-logging instruments, and level gauges can contain sources. Opening the casing exposes the source. They look no different from ordinary metal parts. Do not rely on recognizing a radioactive source: never dismantle, sell, or take home equipment parts of unknown origin. People in China have unknowingly picked up radioactive sources. In May 2014, an iridium-192 source was lost during inspection work at a factory in Nanjing Chemical Industry Park. A warehouse manager found it on his rounds and put it in his work-clothes pocket. He was later diagnosed with mild acute radiation sickness and acute radiation skin injury to his right leg. He spent a year in hospital and still needed two crutches several years later. Two other workers said they had seen it; one thought it was a necklace on his way to work, picked it up, examined it, and threw it away. Tianjin Hongdi Engineering Inspection Development Co., Ltd. lost the source. No official accident notice was found. The injuries of the man who picked it up come from a follow-up paper published by doctors at the Jiangsu Provincial Center for Disease Control and Prevention; the account of someone picking it up and throwing it away comes only from reporting in China Environment News. People working in scrap recycling, dismantling, hardware, and construction face much higher risks than most people. Walk around any cordoned-off construction area marked with the radiation trefoil. A nuclear power plant leak is a different type of accident and is even less likely for an ordinary person to encounter. The main beneficiaries are you and family members at the scene."]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-personal-note"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["My note"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button"},"children":["Write a reminder for yourself…"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"className":"life-tip-p